\PYG{c+cm}{/*}
\PYG{c+cm}{   HOW TO EXTRACT A NEGATIVE CYCLE (If needed)}
\PYG{c+cm}{   If you only need to print ONE negative cycle (like CSES Cycle Finding):}
\PYG{c+cm}{   1. Keep an array `parent`.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   2. Run Bellman\PYGZhy{}Ford for exactly N iterations (no need for Phase 2 above).}
\PYG{c+cm}{   3. On the N\PYGZhy{}th iteration, if an edge (u, v) is relaxed, `v` is either in }
\PYG{c+cm}{      the negative cycle or reachable from it.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   4. To find a node strictly inside the cycle, go back `N` times using `parent`:}
\PYG{c+cm}{      int x = v;}
\PYG{c+cm}{      for (int i = 1; i \PYGZlt{}= n; i++) x = parent[x];}
\PYG{c+cm}{   5. Now `x` is guaranteed to be in the cycle. Trace back using `parent[x]` }
\PYG{c+cm}{      until you reach `x` again, push nodes to a vector, and reverse it.}
\PYG{c+cm}{*/}
\end{MintedVerbatim}
